# Is the control arm a control?
#
# Every other case reads its delta as "what Crewforth changed". That holds only if the bare arm runs without
# Crewforth — and on a machine where Crewforth is installed as a user plugin, or a user-level skill or agent is
# named crew-*, the bare arm used to load it too: the CLI read the user's settings, plugins and MCP servers into
# both arms alike. The runner now isolates both arms and checks each run's opening event; this case asks the
# session itself, as a second, independent reading of the same fact.
#
# Graded on the reply, since the reply IS the artifact here. Both arms are expected to pass: the kit arm must see
# Crewforth (the twin that shows the question can be answered at all), the bare arm must not.

DESC="Does the control arm see no Crewforth component, while the kit arm does?"

seed() {
  printf '# scratch\n' > README.md
}

PROMPT='List by name every subagent type, skill and slash command available to you in this session, one per line, with no explanation. Do not run any tool and do not change any file.'
